1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:24,055
Priya Patel changed her mind: the vanity is now natural oak, not white. Change the job's materials.

2
00:00:24,055 --> 00:00:43,266
Before: everything is white melamine. Note the sheet list.

3
00:00:43,266 --> 00:00:49,516
Materials are set per cabinet. Open the sink cabinet, B1.

4
00:00:49,516 --> 00:00:58,552
Carcass and doors: PB18-OAK, the natural oak melamine with grain.

5
00:00:58,552 --> 00:01:12,313
The edgebanding follows: oak ABS on the carcass front edges and all door edges.

6
00:01:12,313 --> 00:01:34,394
Same for the drawer bank, B2: oak carcass, oak drawer fronts, oak edges.

7
00:01:34,394 --> 00:01:43,738
The drawer boxes stay white: 16 mm white board, the side thickness TANDEM slides are made for.

8
00:01:43,738 --> 00:01:56,039
The cut list regroups by material: oak parts, the white drawer boxes and the backs.

9
00:01:56,039 --> 00:02:00,694
The edgeband totals switch to the oak tape.

10
00:02:00,694 --> 00:02:08,201
Nesting re-runs on its own: oak sheets now, with the grain kept along each part.

11
00:02:08,201 --> 00:02:11,404
A change of finish on a whole job takes a minute, and the cut list, nesting and labels all follow.
